### Backend Service (`server/`)

We will create a Node/Express backend that handles HTTP requests and Socket.IO real-time connections.

#### [NEW] [package.json](file:///d:/project-3/server/package.json)
Backend dependencies: `express`, `mongoose`, `socket.io`, `jsonwebtoken`, `bcryptjs`, `cors`, `multer`, `dotenv`, and `mongodb-memory-server`.

#### [NEW] [server.js](file:///d:/project-3/server/server.js)
The main entry point. Sets up express, server routing, Socket.IO initialization, static asset serving, and handles startup.

#### [NEW] [db.js](file:///d:/project-3/server/config/db.js)
Establishes mongoose connection. If no `MONGODB_URI` is specified in `.env`, spins up `mongodb-memory-server` and connects to it.

#### [NEW] [User.js](file:///d:/project-3/server/models/User.js)
Mongoose model for users: `username`, `email`, `passwordHash`, `avatarUrl`, `status` ('online' or 'offline'), and `lastSeen`.

#### [NEW] [Channel.js](file:///d:/project-3/server/models/Channel.js)
Mongoose model for chat channels/groups: `name` (for group/channel), `isGroup` (true for channels, false for direct messages), `members` (list of User IDs), and `createdBy`.

#### [NEW] [Message.js](file:///d:/project-3/server/models/Message.js)
Mongoose model for messages: `sender` (User ID), `channel` (Channel ID), `content` (text content), `fileUrl`, `fileName`, `fileType`, and `readBy` (array of objects storing user reference and read timestamp).

#### [NEW] [auth.js](file:///d:/project-3/server/middleware/auth.js)
Authentication middleware to extract and verify JWT tokens from requests.

#### [NEW] [auth.js](file:///d:/project-3/server/routes/auth.js)
Routes for `/api/auth/register`, `/api/auth/login`, `/api/auth/me`, and `/api/auth/users` (to list users to DM).

#### [NEW] [channels.js](file:///d:/project-3/server/routes/channels.js)
Routes for `/api/channels` (get all user's channels, create a channel).

#### [NEW] [messages.js](file:///d:/project-3/server/routes/messages.js)
Routes for `/api/messages/:channelId` (retrieve history) and `/api/messages/:channelId/search` (search chat content).

#### [NEW] [upload.js](file:///d:/project-3/server/routes/upload.js)
Handles files uploaded using `multer`, saving files to `/server/uploads/` and returning URLs.

#### [NEW] [socket.js](file:///d:/project-3/server/sockets/socket.js)
Manages Socket.IO events:
- Authentication & association of sockets with user IDs.
- Connection/disconnection presence events (`status: online/offline`).
- Room joining (separate rooms for channels/DMs).
- Messaging events, typing notifications (`typing`, `stop_typing`).
- Read receipt updates.

